# Dovin's Veto counters target noncreature spell. Bot2's Ornithopter is an artifact creature spell, so the Veto is not
# offered against it (refusal); Sol Ring, a plain artifact, is the positive control and is countered. Bot2 answers the
# Veto with Negate: "can't be countered" (CR 101.2 / 701.6) leaves the Veto on the stack, so it still counters Sol Ring.
# The pool is empty right after the cast: exactly {W}{U} was paid (Mox Pearl, Mox Sapphire).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Dovin's Veto
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Negate
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
? Stack = Ornithopter
! Bot1.Hand.Dovin's Veto.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dovin's Veto.Cast(Stack.Sol Ring)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Negate.Cast(Stack.Dovin's Veto)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Sol Ring; Negate
Bot1.Graveyard = Dovin's Veto
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
